source_event: libcdr native r1 graph failure; r2 stale dependency label; r3 independently frozen corrected label and tests PASS 2026-10-13 current CI repair; libcdr-ci-repair-w3-20261013-r1, official CI log SHA256 cd24f4b9b6ad2347b45bcaaa059142d44d1a8a8ab354827482473bca4d0db450; This is not a new base64 transport claim. The increment is preserving consumer test-data identity across a text-only CI diff application path, independently of package/recipe identity. The checksum-verified original parser sample and all assertions remain unchanged. 2026-10-13 current CI repair; libcdr-ci-repair-w3-20261013-r101, official CI log SHA256 cb8b5ed11c5705ae2e9de2a3ee1e8ecaa7fea182ffebfe8a89e59ea8705cef65; Current worker logs provide the independent second-failure boundary after the earlier checkout/fixture repair: successful source retrieval and dependency installation are not proof that configure generated usable config files. Use both-branch source reconciliation, timestamp-preserving production-helper tests and complete native recipe/tests; do not treat a missing-curl predownload warning as the cause when source() already succeeded. This extends the existing evidence/transport topic with a causal validation boundary, not a new generic umask claim. 2026-10-14 current CI repair; libcdr-ci-repair-w3-20261013-r301, official CI log SHA256 69f097174198e763fb36bc86ffe2c53e063b992ef59aa84b2c6dd7e2b36e39a2; Current worker first advanced beyond the repaired config.status boundary and then rejected zlib/1.3.1 zutil.o while linking the real shared producer. Registry version suffix order is not proof of PIC: downloaded zlib/1.3.1.2 remains non-PIC, while 1.3.1.1 explicitly compiles the same upstream source with -fPIC. Bind the published recipe and binary revision before changing the graph, preserve every parser assertion, and validate a real DSO link rather than executable-only zlib smoke tests.

